1
00:00:15,180 --> 00:00:16,897
Destiny. Fate. Dreams.

2
00:00:16,980 --> 00:00:21,140
These unstoppable ideals are
held deep in the heart of man.

3
00:00:21,560 --> 00:00:24,937
As long as there are people
who seek freedom in this life,

4
00:00:25,020 --> 00:00:27,667
these things shall not
vanish from the earth.

5
00:00:34,720 --> 00:00:37,517
People tell me my head's in the clouds.

6
00:00:37,600 --> 00:00:40,877
I don't care what they say
because I'm dreaming of you.

7
00:00:40,960 --> 00:00:43,557
You are the treasure I found.

8
00:00:43,640 --> 00:00:46,657
So bright, so bold, it's so elusive.

9
00:00:46,740 --> 00:00:48,737
It's hard to look away.

10
00:00:48,820 --> 00:00:51,857
Even though it's blinding me.

11
00:00:51,940 --> 00:00:55,677
There are no words to
describe how I feel inside.

12
00:00:55,760 --> 00:00:58,020
I'm really, really stuck on you.

13
00:00:59,220 --> 00:01:02,537
I have to follow my dreams,
however crazy they seem.

14
00:01:02,620 --> 00:01:05,577
And I won't stop till I
get there, you will see.

15
00:01:05,660 --> 00:01:08,877
You're all I need to have
the strength to believe.

16
00:01:08,960 --> 00:01:12,520
Believe in wonderland.

17
00:01:17,880 --> 00:01:21,097
I'm gonna follow my dreams,
however crazy they seem.

18
00:01:21,180 --> 00:01:24,157
I'm gonna share them
with you, a love so true.

19
00:01:24,240 --> 00:01:27,557
You're all I want,
together we can move on.

20
00:01:27,640 --> 00:01:29,917
We live how we want to.

21
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:32,037
There is no limit to us.

22
00:01:32,120 --> 00:01:33,557
We have the power of love.

23
00:01:33,640 --> 00:01:36,617
We don't want to live ordinary life.

24
00:01:36,700 --> 00:01:39,677
We have a chance to live in paradise.

25
00:01:39,760 --> 00:01:42,240
We live in one another.

26
00:01:50,900 --> 00:01:51,940
Baroque Works?

27
00:01:52,120 --> 00:01:56,532
I don't know that I've even heard of
such a company Are you sure it exists?

28
00:01:56,900 --> 00:02:00,440
We're just ordinary citizens
of Alabasta, Mr. Marine.

29
00:02:00,920 --> 00:02:05,214
You wouldn't want to hurt good citizens
just because there's a rebellion.

30
00:02:07,160 --> 00:02:08,857
Wait, Sergeant Major, they...

31
00:02:08,940 --> 00:02:09,770
Shut up!

32
00:02:10,020 --> 00:02:11,902
Why were you hesitating, Marine?

33
00:02:12,500 --> 00:02:15,117
If you wait for proof, you
won't prevent anything.

34
00:02:15,200 --> 00:02:17,937
You should be able to tell
who the enemy is immediately.

35
00:02:18,020 --> 00:02:19,960
Yes, we're very sorry, Sergeant.

36
00:02:20,600 --> 00:02:22,540
We only have until 4.30.

37
00:02:22,840 --> 00:02:24,369
We're running out of time.

38
00:02:26,460 --> 00:02:27,320
The clock.

39
00:02:29,120 --> 00:02:30,437
Robot, Robot, Robot.

40
00:02:30,520 --> 00:02:31,500
Hey, listen, Mr.

41
00:02:31,640 --> 00:02:32,470
Seven.

42
00:02:32,553 --> 00:02:35,757
I think this is a very important
mission the boss has assigned to us.

43
00:02:35,840 --> 00:02:39,537
I think you're absolutely correct
about that, Miss Father's Day.

44
00:02:39,620 --> 00:02:40,917
And do you know what else?

45
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:45,941
I'll bet we'll get big promotions for
pulling this off successfully, Robot, Robot.

46
00:02:46,640 --> 00:02:48,993
I do hope that that is a planned reward.

47
00:02:49,340 --> 00:02:52,177
After all, this is quite a difficult
mission when you think about it,

48
00:02:52,260 --> 00:02:53,090
Miss Father's Day.

49
00:02:53,173 --> 00:02:56,861
We're shooting a cannonball into
the crowd using such a big cannon!

50
00:02:59,560 --> 00:03:01,800
So the reward should be just as big!

51
00:03:06,820 --> 00:03:09,540
Robot, it's almost time
to go now, Mr. Seven!

52
00:03:10,400 --> 00:03:11,900
We're ready to fire!

53
00:03:13,380 --> 00:03:14,210
Yeah!

54
00:03:27,400 --> 00:03:28,871
What is it you're saying?

55
00:03:30,220 --> 00:03:33,573
What is it that you think I
do not understand, Straw Hat?

56
00:03:43,200 --> 00:03:44,120
Kong Kong!

57
00:03:45,280 --> 00:03:46,110
Let me!

58
00:03:54,500 --> 00:03:56,206
I don't think you understand.

59
00:03:56,360 --> 00:03:58,419
You're going to die here very soon.

60
00:03:58,880 --> 00:04:01,645
The poison from my hook
has entered your wound.

61
00:04:04,520 --> 00:04:07,760
Your body is probably
becoming numb right now.

62
00:04:08,980 --> 00:04:11,917
It doesn't matter whether
you win or lose this fight.

63
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:16,177
Your body will still be buried underneath
the rubble when this temple collapses.

64
00:04:16,260 --> 00:04:18,940
Fifteen seconds until we shoot! Oh!

65
00:04:21,140 --> 00:04:24,960
Cannon aimed at the center of
Palace Square, rivet rivet! Oh!

66
00:04:25,520 --> 00:04:26,350
Fire!

67
00:04:27,740 --> 00:04:30,637
Hey, Nami, what the hell is
it you're trying to do anyway?

68
00:04:30,720 --> 00:04:33,057
We really don't have time to play around!

69
00:04:33,140 --> 00:04:35,258
If we mess this up, we're gonna die!

70
00:04:35,420 --> 00:04:36,250
Hey!

71
00:04:36,333 --> 00:04:38,117
Thanks, Usat, but I already know that!

72
00:04:38,200 --> 00:04:40,057
Now just shut up and stand there quietly!

73
00:04:40,140 --> 00:04:41,081
I'm calculating!

74
00:04:41,260 --> 00:04:43,777
Hey, Nami, shut up if I had
any idea what was going on!

75
00:04:43,860 --> 00:04:46,517
Would you just explain what the
hell it is you're planning already?!

76
00:04:46,600 --> 00:04:47,430
Calm down!

77
00:04:47,513 --> 00:04:48,343
You'll know soon enough!

78
00:04:48,426 --> 00:04:49,580
Are you ready?

79
00:04:50,300 --> 00:04:51,537
Robot, Robot, Robot.

80
00:04:51,620 --> 00:04:53,060
Hey, listen, Mr. Seven.

81
00:04:53,260 --> 00:04:54,957
This is a very special occasion.

82
00:04:55,040 --> 00:04:56,981
I think we should do a countdown.

83
00:04:57,340 --> 00:04:59,177
That's a good plan, Miss Father's Day.

84
00:04:59,260 --> 00:05:00,977
A good plan, a very good plan.

85
00:05:01,060 --> 00:05:02,178
Sounds interesting.

86
00:05:03,620 --> 00:05:05,180
Forecasting a typhoon.

87
00:05:05,720 --> 00:05:07,500
Here we go.

88
00:05:08,220 --> 00:05:09,050
Countdown.

89
00:05:11,780 --> 00:05:12,700
Cyclone Tempo!

90
00:05:13,480 --> 00:05:14,840
What? But wait!

91
00:05:15,060 --> 00:05:17,648
Cyclone Tempo is just
a silly boomerang game

92
00:05:18,740 --> 00:05:20,520
Just head for the clock tower!

93
00:05:34,980 --> 00:05:35,820
What the?

94
00:05:36,080 --> 00:05:37,360
They're flying up?

95
00:05:38,560 --> 00:05:39,390
Chopper!

96
00:05:39,473 --> 00:05:41,496
Jump up to where Sanji is, all right?

97
00:05:42,160 --> 00:05:43,320
Huh? That's it?

98
00:05:43,420 --> 00:05:44,737
This is her big plan?

99
00:05:44,820 --> 00:05:47,777
To make it all the way up
there piggyback like this?

100
00:05:47,860 --> 00:05:49,717
Sanji, you know what to do, right?

101
00:05:49,800 --> 00:05:50,860
We have to hurry!

102
00:05:51,220 --> 00:05:53,514
I think I get the idea, but it's risky.

103
00:05:53,660 --> 00:05:55,920
Well, I guess I just have to do it.

104
00:05:56,140 --> 00:05:58,337
It's too late to turn back at this point.

105
00:05:58,420 --> 00:05:59,596
Tony, let's do this.

106
00:05:59,700 --> 00:06:01,994
Okay, Phoebe, now just hang on tightly.

107
00:06:04,140 --> 00:06:04,970
I see.

108
00:06:05,140 --> 00:06:06,577
That's what they're doing.

109
00:06:06,660 --> 00:06:08,440
Chopper, get on my right leg!

110
00:06:11,960 --> 00:06:12,790
11 seconds!

111
00:06:13,860 --> 00:06:14,742
Here they come!

112
00:06:15,840 --> 00:06:17,100
Good job so far.

113
00:06:19,540 --> 00:06:22,600
So I just throw him to the
top of that tower. Turn!

114
00:06:24,980 --> 00:06:25,940
Yeah, I'm ready.

115
00:06:26,040 --> 00:06:26,870
Come on up.

116
00:06:27,680 --> 00:06:28,510
That's what?

117
00:06:28,720 --> 00:06:30,117
It's a flat of the blade.

118
00:06:30,200 --> 00:06:31,030
Calm down.

119
00:06:31,113 --> 00:06:32,560
It's your footing. Okay.

120
00:06:33,300 --> 00:06:34,130
Nine!

121
00:06:34,400 --> 00:06:35,230
Careful.

122
00:06:35,313 --> 00:06:36,857
There's a couple of weirdos up there.

123
00:06:36,940 --> 00:06:38,160
Yes, I know them.

124
00:06:39,880 --> 00:06:40,710
Oops.

125
00:06:40,940 --> 00:06:43,140
Oh, hello, Miss Wednesday.

126
00:06:43,680 --> 00:06:44,817
Rivet, rivet, rivet.

127
00:06:44,900 --> 00:06:48,312
I'd recognize that little
traitor to our company anywhere.

128
00:06:49,040 --> 00:06:49,940
They noticed!

129
00:06:50,360 --> 00:06:51,220
They did?

130
00:06:51,480 --> 00:06:52,833
We're still in the air.

131
00:06:53,020 --> 00:06:54,200
This is really bad.

132
00:06:54,460 --> 00:06:56,578
If they shoot at us, we're finished.

133
00:06:57,700 --> 00:07:00,994
Whatever it is you really
want can't be in this country.

134
00:07:01,380 --> 00:07:02,280
Aren't I right?

135
00:07:02,440 --> 00:07:04,897
You're fighting for
somebody else's goal now.

136
00:07:04,980 --> 00:07:07,517
And how can there be any
point in time for that?

137
00:07:07,600 --> 00:07:09,997
If only you would just get
rid of a friend or two,

138
00:07:10,080 --> 00:07:13,497
you could easily avoid so many
of these inconvenient problems.

139
00:07:13,580 --> 00:07:15,992
Loyalty is only for idiots and weaklings.

140
00:07:17,200 --> 00:07:21,400
Like I said, you really don't
understand anything, do you?

141
00:07:23,540 --> 00:07:24,370
Vivi...

142
00:07:25,720 --> 00:07:29,480
Vivi is always telling people
not to risk their lives.

143
00:07:29,920 --> 00:07:33,508
She's the first to lay down her
life in order to save others.

144
00:07:33,640 --> 00:07:37,500
If we don't help her,
she'll die. You'll kill her.

145
00:07:37,660 --> 00:07:39,260
You still don't get it.

146
00:07:39,940 --> 00:07:41,697
That's what makes her such a burden.

147
00:07:41,780 --> 00:07:44,721
So why not ditch the
princess and save yourselves?

148
00:07:44,900 --> 00:07:47,220
Because none of us want Vivi to die!

149
00:07:47,600 --> 00:07:49,835
Helping each other is what friends do!

150
00:07:49,960 --> 00:07:53,697
And that's why none of us will leave
her behind or quit fighting you!

151
00:07:53,780 --> 00:07:57,486
As long as she doesn't give up
on her country, neither will we!

152
00:07:58,040 --> 00:08:01,040
Even if that means all the
rest of you end up dead?

153
00:08:01,300 --> 00:08:02,740
If we die, we die.

154
00:08:02,900 --> 00:08:04,429
That's all there is to it.

155
00:08:05,120 --> 00:08:07,197
Adjust Ribbit's Ribbit's Gun for attack!

156
00:08:07,280 --> 00:08:08,927
This is an unexpected catch.

157
00:08:09,900 --> 00:08:11,280
Adjusting Yellow Gun!

158
00:08:12,200 --> 00:08:13,520
How nice, how nice.

159
00:08:13,620 --> 00:08:14,450
This is good.

160
00:08:14,533 --> 00:08:15,797
They are the perfect prey for us.

161
00:08:15,880 --> 00:08:17,797
What do you think you bastards are doing?

162
00:08:17,880 --> 00:08:19,586
Pointing your guns at Phoebe!

163
00:08:19,960 --> 00:08:20,790
This isn't good.

164
00:08:20,873 --> 00:08:22,357
The two of them are a sniper team.

165
00:08:22,440 --> 00:08:24,597
Chopper, I'll throw you guys up anyway.

166
00:08:24,680 --> 00:08:27,337
It'll change the direction, but
you need to figure something out.

167
00:08:27,420 --> 00:08:28,660
Huh? What do I do?

168
00:08:28,820 --> 00:08:30,114
We have seven seconds!

169
00:08:30,420 --> 00:08:31,980
Just figure something out!

170
00:08:34,800 --> 00:08:36,624
Chopper, Phoebe, are you ready?

171
00:08:36,760 --> 00:08:37,878
I'm sending you up.

172
00:08:40,280 --> 00:08:41,110
Ready?

173
00:08:41,193 --> 00:08:42,120
Aim and fire!

174
00:08:44,200 --> 00:08:46,900
Our bullets are set to
crash into each other.

175
00:08:47,900 --> 00:08:50,060
And then they're going to explode!

176
00:08:54,240 --> 00:08:55,070
No!

177
00:08:59,560 --> 00:09:00,660
What an idiot!

178
00:09:01,120 --> 00:09:02,060
He's hit!

179
00:09:03,300 --> 00:09:04,476
Are you ready, baby?

180
00:09:04,820 --> 00:09:07,349
Just throw me with all
your strength, Tony!

181
00:09:10,760 --> 00:09:13,040
It's no use, Robot Robot!

182
00:09:13,640 --> 00:09:15,080
I'm in fire!

183
00:09:15,800 --> 00:09:16,760
Who's that?

184
00:09:25,780 --> 00:09:27,740
Where'd Miss Wednesday go?

185
00:09:28,040 --> 00:09:29,420
Oh, what now?

186
00:09:33,080 --> 00:09:34,700
Peacock! String!

187
00:09:35,360 --> 00:09:36,660
Up there!

188
00:09:48,560 --> 00:09:50,377
You can talk as tough as you want!

189
00:09:50,460 --> 00:09:52,637
And keep blathering on about
friendship if you like?

190
00:09:52,720 --> 00:09:55,191
but your body is still freezing up on you.

191
00:09:55,700 --> 00:09:58,040
You look pathetic, Straw Hat.

192
00:10:04,380 --> 00:10:05,210
Blaster!

193
00:10:05,293 --> 00:10:06,123
Fire!

194
00:10:06,206 --> 00:10:07,036
Is that right?

195
00:10:08,540 --> 00:10:09,370
Right!

196
00:10:09,520 --> 00:10:10,500
Well, princess?

197
00:10:10,760 --> 00:10:12,231
Looks like you missed us!

198
00:10:17,860 --> 00:10:18,690
Rush back!

199
00:10:22,660 --> 00:10:23,780
All right!

200
00:10:47,420 --> 00:10:48,520
Vivi!

201
00:10:49,280 --> 00:10:50,110
Hey!

202
00:10:50,320 --> 00:10:51,740
Out of here, you brats!

203
00:10:52,000 --> 00:10:54,257
Did you sneak in through
the shortcut again?

204
00:10:54,340 --> 00:10:55,660
Gatekeeper! Run!

205
00:10:56,500 --> 00:11:00,780
Would the two of you please say
something to the kids to keep them away?

206
00:11:02,240 --> 00:11:03,300
Hmm? Sure.

207
00:11:04,780 --> 00:11:06,520
Vivi, going somewhere?

208
00:11:07,480 --> 00:11:09,360
The secret phase. Right.

209
00:11:09,780 --> 00:11:11,368
Well, you have a good time.

210
00:11:13,680 --> 00:11:16,440
So, where did Princess Vivi go?

211
00:11:17,000 --> 00:11:17,830
Huh?

212
00:11:17,913 --> 00:11:20,100
Oh, I can't tell you. It's a secret.

213
00:11:21,640 --> 00:11:23,160
The clock tower, huh?

214
00:11:54,240 --> 00:11:56,040
It stopped, right?

215
00:12:21,440 --> 00:12:22,880
Oh, hey.

216
00:12:23,160 --> 00:12:24,278
You're still alive.

217
00:12:25,500 --> 00:12:26,330
Yeah.

218
00:12:26,413 --> 00:12:27,805
What happened with the cannon?

219
00:12:29,520 --> 00:12:30,880
What was that?

220
00:12:36,580 --> 00:12:37,639
What's the matter?

221
00:12:38,140 --> 00:12:40,117
Apparently something's
gone wrong up there.

222
00:12:40,200 --> 00:12:41,030
It's Vivi.

223
00:12:41,120 --> 00:12:42,649
We still haven't seen her.

224
00:12:44,960 --> 00:12:46,620
Oh, no! You guys!

225
00:12:46,980 --> 00:12:47,960
What is it?

226
00:12:48,260 --> 00:12:50,177
The cannonball has a timing device.

227
00:12:50,260 --> 00:12:52,613
If we don't do something, it'll explode!

228
00:12:53,560 --> 00:12:55,060
What did you say?

229
00:12:58,400 --> 00:13:00,280
A time bomb? No.

230
00:13:03,740 --> 00:13:05,900
I was very well prepared, Cobra.

231
00:13:06,060 --> 00:13:08,977
You have to be willing to
admit that much, surely.

232
00:13:09,060 --> 00:13:13,354
The most successful missions always
account for unforeseen circumstances.

233
00:13:14,720 --> 00:13:18,817
In this case, for instance, even if
something happens to the cannoneers,

234
00:13:18,900 --> 00:13:21,477
the cannonball will
still explode on its own.

235
00:13:21,560 --> 00:13:24,795
The attack will only be
delayed by a few seconds or so.

236
00:13:25,940 --> 00:13:30,197
Of course, I did originally want it to
be shot into the center of the square.

237
00:13:30,280 --> 00:13:32,257
But the cannonball is
big enough that it should

238
00:13:32,340 --> 00:13:34,869
do plenty of damage
from right where it is.

239
00:13:41,260 --> 00:13:42,613
Stopping the rebellion.

240
00:13:43,000 --> 00:13:44,180
Saving the kingdom.

241
00:13:44,600 --> 00:13:47,860
All those worthless ideas
you've clung to for so long.

242
00:13:49,640 --> 00:13:53,040
In the end, they just
created more victims for me.

243
00:13:58,560 --> 00:14:00,480
Let me tell you something.

244
00:14:05,940 --> 00:14:08,740
You're never going to save this country.

245
00:14:12,560 --> 00:14:14,040
Dammit, this isn't right!

246
00:14:14,360 --> 00:14:17,197
Stopping the cannoneers should
have stopped the attack!

247
00:14:17,280 --> 00:14:18,360
A timer?

248
00:14:19,460 --> 00:14:22,217
Considering its power, even
if it explodes from up there,

249
00:14:22,300 --> 00:14:25,888
It will still kill all the people
in the square and the town?

250
00:14:27,500 --> 00:14:29,277
Then what's going to happen now?

251
00:14:29,360 --> 00:14:30,190
Oh crap,

252
00:14:30,273 --> 00:14:31,897
does this mean it was impossible all along

253
00:14:31,980 --> 00:14:34,568
for us to stop the
explosion from happening?

254
00:14:37,840 --> 00:14:40,677
He made us spend all
this time looking for it.

255
00:14:40,760 --> 00:14:43,997
He even announced the attack
so we would do just that!

256
00:14:44,080 --> 00:14:45,100
Why?

257
00:14:48,820 --> 00:14:53,420
Just how far will Crocodile insist
on going to make fools of us all?

258
00:14:54,740 --> 00:14:57,357
It's not enough for him to
tear this country apart!

259
00:14:57,440 --> 00:14:59,675
He has to mock us while he's doing it!

260
00:15:02,820 --> 00:15:03,650
Crocodile!

261
00:15:15,700 --> 00:15:19,477
And that's why none of us will leave
her behind or quit fighting you!

262
00:15:19,560 --> 00:15:23,266
As long as she doesn't give up
on her country, neither will we!

263
00:15:42,620 --> 00:15:44,597
You can't

264
00:15:44,680 --> 00:15:50,360
defeat me!

265
00:15:52,840 --> 00:15:56,899
